{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Nuclear power stations use controlled fission reactions to release energy from nuclear fuel. The energy heats water or another coolant, enabling steam to drive turbines and generators. Nuclear power produces very low direct carbon dioxide emissions during operation and can provide large amounts of controllable electricity. However, power stations are expensive to build and decommission, radioactive waste requires careful long-term management, and safety systems are essential. The amount of energy released per kilogram of nuclear fuel is very high, but this does not make the resource infinite.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": true}", "duration": 41.822041, "words": [["Nuclear", 0.0], ["power", 0.557], ["stations", 0.906], ["use", 1.637], ["controlled", 1.95], ["fission", 2.682], ["reactions", 3.216], ["to", 3.866], ["release", 4.04], ["energy", 4.447], ["from", 5.016], ["nuclear", 5.306], ["fuel.", 5.817], ["The", 6.455], ["energy", 6.687], ["heats", 7.175], ["water", 7.512], ["or", 8.022], ["another", 8.313], ["coolant,", 8.8], ["enabling", 9.427], ["steam", 10.054], ["to", 10.495], ["drive", 10.646], ["turbines", 11.018], ["and", 11.691], ["generators.", 11.935], ["Nuclear", 13.154], ["power", 13.723], ["produces", 14.118], ["very", 14.733], ["low", 15.105], ["direct", 15.546], ["carbon", 16.126], ["dioxide", 16.637], ["emissions", 17.322], ["during", 17.96], ["operation", 18.436], ["and", 19.33], ["can", 19.644], ["provide", 19.864], ["large", 20.352], ["amounts", 20.642], ["of", 21.095], ["controllable", 21.316], ["electricity.", 22.059], ["However,", 23.104], ["power", 23.742], ["stations", 24.114], ["are", 24.741], ["expensive", 25.008], ["to", 25.623], ["build", 25.774], ["and", 26.157], ["decommission,", 26.436], ["radioactive", 27.48], ["waste", 28.432], ["requires", 28.967], ["careful", 29.628], ["long-term", 30.151], ["management,", 30.696], ["and", 31.579], ["safety", 31.858], ["systems", 32.36